+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
+## `aesop_ss`
+
+``` hol4
+aesopData.aesop_ss : unit -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Returns Aesop's independently derived tracked simplifier default.
+
+The base is the explicitly prepared `trackedAutoDefaults` provider, not
+ordinary `srw_ss ()` and not the split-enabled `clasimp_ss ()`. Derivation
+weakens conditional congruence, installs ETA matching, fixes conditional
+depth at 40, and replaces both solver lists with Aesop's selected safe and
+unsafe solvers. The additive `[aesop_simp]` rewrites are then installed.
+Splitting remains the search engine's responsibility.
+
+Typed base updates derive eagerly through `trackedAutoDefaults`.
+Attribute-only changes invalidate the derived result by rewrite-list
+identity; unchanged base/rewrite inputs reuse the installed tracked set.
+The provider, derived values and attribute cache follow `Context.restore`.
+No getter promotes or reconstructs an ordinary compiled simpset.
+
+Use `trackedAutoDefaults.with_simpset_updates` for scoped typed updates.
+Ordinary `BasicProvers.with_simpset_updates` remains independent.
+
+### Failure
+
+Fails if the context predates explicit tracked-provider preparation or
+registered derivation, rather than falling back to ordinary state.
+
+### See also
+
+[`aesopLib.AESOP_TAC`](#aesopLib.AESOP_TAC),
+[`aesopLib.CS_AESOP_TAC`](#aesopLib.CS_AESOP_TAC)
