diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.del_looper.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.del_looper.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..464eb0f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.del_looper.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
+## `del_looper`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.del_looper :
+  string -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Removes a named tactic looper from a simpset.
+
+A call to `del_looper name ss` returns a new simpset without the looper
+whose registration name is exactly `name`.  Other loopers retain their
+relative order.  If a looper with that name is subsequently added again,
+it is new at that point and is appended after the remaining loopers.
+
+The removal is recorded as a simpset strategy update, so it is preserved
+when later operations rebuild the simpset from its fragment history.
+The operation does not remove rewrite rules, solvers, or a simpset
+fragment merely because one of them has the same name.
+
+For a temporary alternative, `ExclX ("looper:" ^ name)` in a simplification
+tactic's theorem list suppresses the matching looper for that invocation
+only.  This is often preferable when the looper should remain available
+in the reusable simpset.
+
+Loopers run only after rewriting and final solving have failed.  The
+first applicable looper is used, and simplification restarts on all of
+its subgoals. The bound set by `simpExtLib.limit` caps successful
+looper rounds across the whole tactic invocation.  Removing a looper
+therefore also removes its participation in this ordered, bounded loop.
+
+This operation affects tactic simplification only.  Loopers do not cross
+into `SIMP_CONV`, `SIMP_PROVE`, `SIMP_RULE`, or `ASM_SIMP_RULE`, whether
+or not they are present in the simpset.
+
+### Failure
+
+If no looper has the given name, `del_looper` issues a HOL warning and
+returns the original simpset unchanged.  It does not raise an exception
+for that case.
+
+### Example
+
+``` hol4
+val with_split =
+  simpExtLib.add_looper
+    ("split conjunctions", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
+    simpExtLib.empty_ss
+
+val without_split =
+  simpExtLib.del_looper "split conjunctions" with_split
+```
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.add_looper`](#simpExtLib.add_looper),
+[`simpExtLib.set_looper`](#simpExtLib.set_looper),
+[`simpExtLib.looper_ss`](#simpExtLib.looper_ss)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.del_split.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.del_split.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0b2e88f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.del_split.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
+## `del_split`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.del_split :
+  string -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Removes a named split looper from a simpset.
+
+For an unprefixed argument `name`, a call `del_split name ss` looks for
+both `"split " ^ name` and `"split_asm " ^ name` and removes whichever
+are present. The name is normally a fully qualified theorem database
+name such as `pickTheory$pick_split`.
+
+An argument already beginning with `"split "` or `"split_asm "` is
+treated as an exact strategy name, so only that one looper is considered.
+No theory qualification or short-name expansion is otherwise performed.
+
+Only the returned simpset is changed. In particular, `del_split` does
+not remove a theorem registered in the persistent `[split]` set used by
+[`simpExtLib.split_ss`](#simpExtLib.split_ss). Suppress a dynamically
+selected rule for one invocation with `simpExtLib.ExclX "split:thy$name"`,
+not literal ordinary `Excl`.
+
+### Failure
+
+Never fails. If no candidate strategy name is present, the original
+simpset is returned without a warning.
+
+### Example
+
+Continuing with a simpset containing the stored conclusion rule
+`pickTheory$pick_split`:
+
+``` hol4
+val without_pick =
+  simpExtLib.del_split "pickTheory$pick_split" pick_ss;
+
+(* This exact form removes only the conclusion-rule strategy. *)
+val also_without_pick =
+  simpExtLib.del_split "split pickTheory$pick_split" pick_ss;
+```
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.add_split`](#simpExtLib.add_split),
+[`simpExtLib.split_ss`](#simpExtLib.split_ss),
+[`simpExtLib.Split`](#simpExtLib.Split),
+[`simpExtLib.del_looper`](#simpExtLib.del_looper)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.filter_rewrites.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.filter_rewrites.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a082bd8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.filter_rewrites.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
+## `filter_rewrites`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.filter_rewrites :
+  ((simpExtLib.thname option * thm) -> bool) ->
+  simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Removes the rewrite rules a predicate rejects from a simpset.
+
+A call to `filter_rewrites keep ss` returns a simpset that is the same
+as `ss` except that every rewrite rule for which `keep` returns false
+is gone.  The predicate sees each rule as it was added: its theorem,
+and the name it was added under where it has one.  Conversions,
+congruences, decision procedures, loopers and the simpset's strategy
+settings are left alone.
+
+The result is built by replaying the simpset's history, so everything
+the simpset carries beyond its fragments — the rules it has excluded by
+name with `remove_simps` or `-*`, its fragment exclusions, its limit,
+its rewrite maker, its strategy events — stands in the result as it
+stood in `ss`.  Rebuilding a filtered simpset out of `ssfrags_of`
+instead does not preserve them: the fragments a simpset was built from
+are not the simpset.
+
+Where `keep` rejects nothing, the simpset itself is returned.
+
+### Failure
+
+Never fails, and never raises `Conv.UNCHANGED`.
+
+### Example
+
+Withholding one particular theorem from an otherwise ambient simpset,
+whatever fragment it arrived in:
+
+``` hol4
+val without_thm =
+  simpExtLib.filter_rewrites
+    (fn (_, th) => not (aconv (concl th) (concl unwanted)))
+    (trackedAutoDefaults.base ())
+```
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.remove_ssfrags`](#simpExtLib.remove_ssfrags),
+[`simpExtLib.remove_simps`](#simpExtLib.remove_simps),
+[`simpExtLib.clear_rules`](#simpExtLib.clear_rules),
+[`simpExtLib.mk_simpset`](#simpExtLib.mk_simpset)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.looper_ss.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.looper_ss.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0a14d1f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.looper_ss.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
+## `looper_ss`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.looper_ss :
+  string * (simpExtLib.simpset -> tactic) -> simpExtLib.ssfrag
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Packages one named tactic looper as a simpset fragment.
+
+A call to `looper_ss (name, make_tac)` creates an anonymous `ssfrag` that
+contains the looper and no rewrite rules, conversions, congruences,
+decision procedures, or solvers.  It can be merged into a simpset with
+`++`, or combined with other fragments using `merge_ss`.
+
+When a fragment is merged, looper registration follows the same rules as
+`add_looper`.  A new name is appended after existing loopers.  An
+existing name is updated in place, retaining its priority.  Multiple
+loopers in merged fragments are processed in fragment-list order.  At
+run time the first applicable registered looper is selected.
+
+The function `make_tac` is passed the active, per-invocation simpset.  Its
+tactic is tried only after ordinary rewriting and final solvers fail.
+If it succeeds, the complete simplifier sequence is restarted on each
+subgoal.  It must fail when inapplicable and must make progress whenever
+it succeeds; `Conv.UNCHANGED` is interpreted as failure.
+
+The bound installed by `simpExtLib.limit n` permits at most `n`
+successful looper rounds in one top-level simplification-tactic call.
+The counter is shared by all subgoals.  With no bound, a looper that
+succeeds without progress may diverge.
+
+The looper registration name is independent of the fragment name.  The
+result of `looper_ss` is anonymous; apply `name_ss` if the fragment must
+be removable with `remove_ssfrags` or suppressible with `ExclSF`.
+Regardless of fragment name, `ExclX ("looper:" ^ name)` suppresses this
+looper for one theorem-list invocation.
+
+Looper payloads are tactic hooks.  They are used by simplification
+tactics based on `GEN_SIMP_TAC`, but ignored by the conversion and rule
+interfaces `SIMP_CONV`, `SIMP_PROVE`, `SIMP_RULE`, and `ASM_SIMP_RULE`.
+
+### Failure
+
+`looper_ss` never fails and does not run the supplied function.  Giving
+the resulting anonymous fragment to an operation that requires a named
+fragment can fail unless it has first been passed through `name_ss`.
+
+### Example
+
+``` hol4
+val CONJ_LOOP_ss =
+  simpExtLib.looper_ss
+    ("split conjunctions", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
+  |> simpExtLib.name_ss "CONJ_LOOP"
+
+val ss = simpExtLib.++ (simpExtLib.empty_ss, CONJ_LOOP_ss)
+```
+
+Here `ExclX "looper:split conjunctions"` disables the tactic, retaining the
+fragment.  `ExclSF "CONJ_LOOP"` removes the named fragment, including
+its looper, for that invocation.
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.add_looper`](#simpExtLib.add_looper),
+[`simpExtLib.del_looper`](#simpExtLib.del_looper),
+[`simpExtLib.set_looper`](#simpExtLib.set_looper),
+[`simpExtLib.SSFRAG`](#simpExtLib.SSFRAG),
+[`simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV`](#simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0bc319b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"}; open simpExtLib;
+## `mk_tactic_solver`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver : string * tactic -> TraverseExt.ssolver
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Adapts a tactic into a named simplifier solver.
+
+`mk_tactic_solver (name,tac)` returns a solver named `name`. When asked
+to prove a condition `c`, the solver runs `tac` to completion on the
+goal
+
+``` hol4
+(map concl context_thms, c)
+```
+
+where `context_thms` is the theorem context supplied by the simplifier.
+It then uses `PROVE_HYP` with the actual context theorems. This replaces
+the temporary assumptions introduced for `TAC_PROOF` and preserves any
+hypotheses on which those context theorems themselves depend. The
+solver's `stack` and `recurse` context fields are not used by this
+adapter.
+
+The tactic must solve its goal completely. The resulting solver can be
+registered directly with `add_unsafe_solver` or `add_safe_solver`, or
+packaged in a fragment with `solver_ss` or `safe_solver_ss`.
+
+### Failure
+
+Constructing the solver never fails. At use time, a `HOL_ERR` from the
+tactic is treated as solver non-applicability, so the pipeline can try
+its next solver; other exceptions propagate.
+
+### Example
+
+``` hol4
+val assumption_solver =
+  simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver
+    ("assumption", FIRST_ASSUM ACCEPT_TAC);
+
+val ss =
+  simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver assumption_solver
+    (trackedSimpDefaults.initial_seed ());
+```
+
+This solver can close a side condition that one of the simplifier's
+context theorems proves exactly.
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.add_safe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_safe_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.solver_ss`](#simpExtLib.solver_ss),
+[`simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss`](#simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss),
+[`simpExtLib.set_subgoaler`](#simpExtLib.set_subgoaler)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.remove_solver.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.remove_solver.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8eb9198
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.remove_solver.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"}; open simpExtLib;
+## `remove_solver`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.remove_solver :
+  string -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Removes a named solver from a simpset.
+
+`remove_solver name ss` removes every entry called `name` from both the
+safe and unsafe solver lists of `ss`. If neither list contains `name`,
+the simpset is returned unchanged and no warning is issued.
+
+This operation is persistent on the returned simpset. To suppress a
+named solver for one invocation, pass `ExclX ("solver:" ^ name)` in
+that invocation's theorem list.
+
+### Failure
+
+Never fails.
+
+### Example
+
+``` hol4
+val ss_without_arithmetic =
+  simpExtLib.remove_solver "linear arithmetic" ss;
+```
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.add_safe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_safe_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.set_unsafe_solvers`](#simpExtLib.set_unsafe_solvers),
+[`simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers`](#simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..063cfda
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"}; open simpExtLib;
+## `safe_solver_ss`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss : TraverseExt.ssolver -> simpExtLib.ssfrag
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Creates a simpset fragment containing one safe solver.
+
+`safe_solver_ss solver` is an anonymous fragment with `solver` in its
+safe solver list and no other simplification components. Adding the
+fragment to a simpset with `++` appends the solver unless that simpset's
+safe list already contains the same name. No duplicate active entry is
+created, and registration order is preserved.
+
+Once merged, the solver is available as a final solver to
+`GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe=true}`. It is not used for conditional-rewrite side
+conditions inside the simplifier engine. Those always use unsafe
+solvers, which can be packaged with `solver_ss`.
+
+Use `name_ss` if the fragment must later be identifiable by
+`remove_ssfrags` or `exclude_ssfrags`.
+
+### Failure
+
+Never fails.
+
+### Example
+
+``` hol4
+val assumption_solver =
+  simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver
+    ("safe assumption", FIRST_ASSUM ACCEPT_TAC);
+
+val safe_assumption_ss =
+  simpExtLib.name_ss "safe assumption solver"
+    (simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss assumption_solver);
+```
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.solver_ss`](#simpExtLib.solver_ss),
+[`simpExtLib.add_safe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_safe_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver`](#simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.remove_ssfrags`](#simpExtLib.remove_ssfrags)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_cond_depth.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_cond_depth.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6947d11
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_cond_depth.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
+## `set_cond_depth`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.set_cond_depth :
+  int -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Sets the side-condition stack limit for invocations of a simpset.
+
+A call to `set_cond_depth n ss` returns a copy of `ss` whose simplifier
+traversals use `n` as the limit on nested conditions generated by
+conditional rewrites.  A conditional rewrite is skipped when adding all
+of its conditions would make the current side-condition stack longer
+than `n`.  Thus, increasing the value can allow deeply nested chains of
+conditional rewrites to succeed, but can also permit more work or
+non-termination.
+
+The setting is passed explicitly in the extension traversal configuration;
+no global reference is mutated, even during nested calls or exceptions.
+An unconfigured simpset retains `NONE`, reading the shared public
+`!Cond_rewr.stack_limit` at each condition check. That reference is
+initially `4`. Configured `SOME n` instead fixes the depth for this set.
+
+There is no special validation of `n`.  A value of zero rejects every
+rewrite having a condition.  A negative value makes even a rewrite with
+no conditions exceed the limit.
+
+### Failure
+
+Never fails.  Rewrites whose conditions exceed the limit are ignored;
+the simplifier invocation does not fail for that reason.
+
+### Example
+
+The following schematic configuration gives a collection of conditional
+rules room for a deeper side-condition chain without changing the
+global reference.
+
+``` hol4
+val deep_ss = simpExtLib.set_cond_depth 40
+  (trackedSimpDefaults.initial_seed ())
+val deep_tac = simpExtLib.SIMP_TAC deep_ss conditional_rules
+```
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.set_term_ord`](#simpExtLib.set_term_ord),
+[`simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV`](#simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV),
+[`simpExtLib.clear_rules`](#simpExtLib.clear_rules)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_looper.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_looper.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..827ec05
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_looper.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
+## `set_looper`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.set_looper :
+  string * (simpExtLib.simpset -> tactic) ->
+  simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Replaces all tactic loopers in a simpset with one named looper.
+
+A call to `set_looper (name, make_tac) ss` returns a new simpset whose
+looper list consists only of `(name, make_tac)`.  Rewrite rules, safe and
+unsafe solvers, and the other simpset strategy settings are unchanged.
+The replacement is recorded as a strategy update and survives later
+rebuilding of the simpset from fragment history.
+
+The supplied function receives the active simpset and returns a tactic.
+After rewriting and final solving fail, that tactic is tried.  On
+success the simplifier restarts rewriting, solving, and looping on every
+resulting subgoal.  The tactic must fail when inapplicable and must not
+succeed without progress; otherwise an unlimited simpset can loop.  A
+`Conv.UNCHANGED` exception is treated as tactic failure.
+
+`set_looper` discards registration order because it creates a singleton
+list.  A later `add_looper` with a different name appends after this
+looper; a later addition with the same name updates it in place.
+
+The bound set by `simpExtLib.limit n` permits at most `n` successful looper
+rounds during one top-level simplification-tactic call, shared over all
+subgoals. `ExclX ("looper:" ^ name)` in the theorem list suppresses
+the singleton looper, without changing the simpset returned here.
+
+Loopers belong to the tactic layer used by `GEN_SIMP_TAC` and its
+clients.  They are not invoked by `SIMP_CONV`, `SIMP_PROVE`, `SIMP_RULE`,
+or `ASM_SIMP_RULE`.
+
+### Failure
+
+`set_looper` itself never fails and does not run the supplied function.
+A later simplification tactic may diverge if the looper repeatedly
+succeeds without progress and no finite limit is installed.
+
+### Example
+
+``` hol4
+val conjunction_only =
+  simpExtLib.set_looper
+    ("split conjunctions", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
+    an_existing_simpset
+```
+
+The result has no loopers inherited from `an_existing_simpset`; only
+`"split conjunctions"` remains.
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.add_looper`](#simpExtLib.add_looper),
+[`simpExtLib.del_looper`](#simpExtLib.del_looper),
+[`simpExtLib.looper_ss`](#simpExtLib.looper_ss),
+[`simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV`](#simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4d313dd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"}; open simpExtLib;
+## `set_safe_solvers`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers :
+  TraverseExt.ssolver list -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Replaces a simpset's safe solver list.
+
+`set_safe_solvers solvers ss` returns a version of `ss` whose safe
+solver list is `solvers`. Duplicate names are removed: the first entry
+with each name is retained, and the order of those first entries is
+preserved. The unsafe solver list is unchanged. Passing `[]` disables
+all safe final solvers.
+
+Safe solvers are tried on the whole residual goal after rewriting by
+`GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe=true}`. They are not used for simplifier-engine side
+conditions. See `add_unsafe_solver` for the distinction between the
+engine and final-solver roles.
+
+### Failure
+
+Never fails.
+
+### Example
+
+``` hol4
+val ss_without_safe_solvers =
+  simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers [] ss;
+```
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.add_safe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_safe_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.set_unsafe_solvers`](#simpExtLib.set_unsafe_solvers),
+[`simpExtLib.remove_solver`](#simpExtLib.remove_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_subgoaler.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_subgoaler.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f4128c8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_subgoaler.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"}; open simpExtLib;
+## `set_subgoaler`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.set_subgoaler :
+  TraverseExt.subgoaler -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Sets the procedure that preprocesses simplifier side conditions.
+
+A `TraverseExt.subgoaler` has type
+
+``` hol4
+TraverseExt.simp_prover_ctxt -> term -> thm
+```
+
+Given a prover context and a condition `c`, it must return an equality
+of the form `|- c = c'`. The context contains the current
+side-condition stack, the available context theorems, and a `recurse`
+function which recursively simplifies a term under that same context.
+
+When a conditional rewrite requests a proof of `c`, the configured
+subgoaler is called first. If its result is `|- c = T`, the condition is
+solved. Otherwise the simpset's unsafe solvers are tried, in order, on
+`c'`; a proof of `c'` is transported through the equality to prove `c`.
+Thus a subgoaler may normalize a condition into a form suitable for a
+specialized solver, rather than proving the condition outright.
+
+`set_subgoaler subgoaler ss` replaces any subgoaler already configured
+on `ss`. The setting affects side conditions in `SIMP_CONV` and in the
+rewrite phase of simplification tactics. It does not configure a
+separate tactic-layer final solver.
+
+If no subgoaler is configured, recursive simplification itself is used.
+There is currently no public operation for restoring `NONE`; retain the
+original simpset if both configured and unconfigured variants are
+needed.
+
+### Failure
+
+`set_subgoaler` itself never fails. At use time, a malformed equality or
+an exception from the subgoaler causes the surrounding side-condition
+attempt to fail or propagate according to the exception involved.
+
+### Example
+
+A subgoaler that explicitly selects the standard recursive
+simplification is:
+
+``` hol4
+fun recursive_subgoaler
+      ({recurse,...} : TraverseExt.simp_prover_ctxt) condition =
+  recurse condition;
+
+val ss' = simpExtLib.set_subgoaler recursive_subgoaler ss;
+```
+
+More specialized subgoalers can inspect `stack` and `context_thms`
+before calling `recurse`.
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver`](#simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver),
+[`simpExtLib.set_cond_depth`](#simpExtLib.set_cond_depth),
+[`simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV`](#simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_term_ord.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_term_ord.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..477b222
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_term_ord.smd
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
+## `set_term_ord`
+
+``` hol4
+simpExtLib.set_term_ord :
+  (term * term -> order) -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
+```
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Sets the term ordering used for permutative rewrites in a simpset.
+
+A rewrite is permutative when its two sides differ only by a permutation
+of variables, as with commutativity.  For an instantiated permutative
+rewrite with left- and right-hand sides `l` and `r`, the simplifier
+applies the rewrite only when the configured function returns
+`GREATER` on `(l,r)`.  The ordering should be a total, AC-compatible
+term ordering; an unsuitable function can prevent normalization or
+make it unstable.
+
+The ordering is passed explicitly in the extension traversal configuration.
+No global reference is mutated, even during nested calls or exceptions.
+An unconfigured simpset uses `Cond_rewr.ac_term_ord`.
+
+The ordering guard is deliberately bypassed for bounded rewrites, such
+as rules marked with `Once` or `Ntimes`: their usage bound prevents the
+unrestricted permutative loop that the ordering normally avoids.
+Non-permutative rewrites are also unaffected by this setting.
+
+### Failure
+
+Never fails.  A permutative rewrite rejected by the ordering is simply
+not applied.  Exceptions raised by the supplied ordering function can
+propagate when the simpset is used.
+
+### Example
+
+This schematic example reverses the standard order and stores the
+resulting policy in a new simpset.
+
+``` hol4
+fun reverse_order pair =
+  case Cond_rewr.ac_term_ord pair of
+      LESS => GREATER
+    | EQUAL => EQUAL
+    | GREATER => LESS
+
+val reverse_ss = simpExtLib.set_term_ord reverse_order
+  (trackedSimpDefaults.initial_seed ())
+```
+
+### See also
+
+[`simpExtLib.set_cond_depth`](#simpExtLib.set_cond_depth),
+[`BoundedRewrites.Once`](#BoundedRewrites.Once),
+[`BoundedRewrites.Ntimes`](#BoundedRewrites.Ntimes),
+[`simpExtLib.clear_rules`](#simpExtLib.clear_rules)
diff --git a/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_unsafe_solvers.smd b/help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.set_unsafe_solvers.smd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7b28859
--- /dev/null
